{"repositoryId":1325995489,"availability":"available","full":"Slottwin517/qapla","name":"qapla","description":"Train a transformer from scratch on an ESP32-S3, no GPU required.","category":"Business","language":"C","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-06T23:36:01Z","updated":"2026-10-12T18:56:13Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://slottwin517.github.io","topics":["ai-agent","bison","c","carrier","cfg","claude-code","ecommerce","ergogen","flask","interpreter","lex","logistics","mysql","programming-language-interpreter","qapla","rest-api","shipping-api","tracking"],"demo":"https://slottwin517.github.io/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:41.721Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:41.721Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:41.721Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T19:08:41.721Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Qapla is a small program that teaches a computer how to predict text. It learns by looking at examples you give it, figuring out patterns, and then generating new text that looks similar. The amazing part? It runs entirely on a tiny ESP32-S3 chip that costs only $8 - no internet connection or powerful computer needed. You'll see artificial intelligence happening right on your desk!","Qapla is doing real artificial intelligence training! It might take hours or days to learn well. This is normal - AI training is intensive work, even on a small chip.","This makes qapla unique! It proves that AI training can happen on extremely limited hardware - no cloud servers, no powerful GPUs, just a $8 chip with 8 MB of memory."],"features":["Transformer neural network - The same type of AI used in ChatGPT, but tiny enough to fit on a microcontroller","Hand-written backpropagation - The training math was written manually in C, not using any pre-built AI libraries"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Slottwin517/qapla/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"